# Mudita Hospital

Offline LAN hospital: **Go + SQLite API** (`server/`) · **Tauri 2 + React** clinic (`client/`) · Admin dashboard (`dashboard/`).

## Start here

Developer standards index: `docs/standards/README.md`  
New domain playbook: `docs/standards/ADDING_A_FEATURE.md`  
Architecture: `docs/standards/ARCHITECTURE.md`

Read only the standard that matches the task. Do not load all of `docs/` unless the task is deploy/ops.

## Monorepo map

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `server/` | API, SQLite, migrations, auth |
| `client/` | Clinic desktop UI |
| `dashboard/` | Admin analytics UI |
| `docs/standards/` | Engineering standards |
| `docs/` (root) | Deploy / field ops only |
| `scripts/`, `deploy/` | Run & package |

## Hard don'ts

- Clients never open SQLite
- Do not commit secrets, PHI DBs, or `dist/`
- Do not add React Router, Redux/Zustand/React Query, or Gin/chi unless explicitly decided
- Match the nearest existing domain (OPD / OT / Pharmacy) instead of inventing a new pattern
- New clinic UI goes in `pages/` / `features/` — do not grow `app/App.tsx` with new panels
- A hospital install is live: keep `data\mudita.db`; ship code around it
- Schema changes are new migrations that keep existing rows — read `docs/standards/UPGRADES.md` before schema or upgrade work
